                        "glosses": [
                            "A long firearm with four barrels (typically two shotgun barrels and two rifle barrels)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "adfa27d6-7684-44e2-9bac-9f7aae65c35c",
                                "sense_id": "5b662e37-88cd-35a0-a8c2-b6edc1f0f957",
                                "text": "The vierling gun that Alan Tuck hunts with is truly a handcrafted work of art."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2b8f6b5-b7fb-48df-8f9e-bf11843099bf",
                                "sense_id": "5b662e37-88cd-35a0-a8c2-b6edc1f0f957",
                                "text": "The Blaser D99 drilling can be custom made with two side-by-side shotgun barrels and a rifle barrel over them. Another variation on the multiple barrel shotgun is the vierling, which is the German word for quadruplet. A vierling has four barrels […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ddf8668a-9634-4120-849a-802ccf8173a1",
                                "sense_id": "5b662e37-88cd-35a0-a8c2-b6edc1f0f957",
                                "text": "2018, James Ballou, Arming for the Apocalypse: Assembling Your Survival Arsenal ... While You Still Can, Prepper Press\n[…] three-barreled drillings, the two-barreled shotgun/rifle cape guns, and the four-barreled vierlings, which all featured some combination of rifle with shotgun barrels within the same gun."
                            }
                        ]
